WEBVTT

00:06.880 --> 00:07.690
Syo-chan.

00:08.710 --> 00:11.070
Since everyone else has been working so hard,

00:11.330 --> 00:14.820
I wrote that I'd do my best
on my duet project that starts tomorrow.

00:14.820 --> 00:16.160
Great idea.

00:16.160 --> 00:16.770
I know.

00:17.280 --> 00:19.870
Once I accomplish my goals,
I put Piyo-chan stickers next to them.

00:19.870 --> 00:22.290
Then you'd better do
your best on this project, too.

00:22.290 --> 00:23.330
Yeah.

02:05.090 --> 02:07.850
Since Mikado Nagi, the cutest boy
in the universe, will be singing,

02:07.850 --> 02:11.950
I want you to write a song that
everyone who hears it will agree is cute.

02:11.950 --> 02:13.390
Great idea.

02:13.390 --> 02:16.360
Cute songs make you so happy.

02:16.700 --> 02:18.040
What are you talking about?

02:18.040 --> 02:20.810
Don't you have any of your own principles?

02:20.810 --> 02:25.580
I'm just happy to sing one of
Haru-chan's songs with you, Nagi-kun.

02:26.440 --> 02:29.490
I've had enough of you, goody two-shoes.

02:29.490 --> 02:30.170
What?

02:30.570 --> 02:35.800
Since everyone expects us to be cute,
I want to include something surprising, too.

02:35.800 --> 02:36.960
For example...

02:36.960 --> 02:39.830
We could play musical instruments.

02:39.830 --> 02:42.390
A live performance would excite the fans,

02:42.390 --> 02:44.720
and everyone would be looking at my cute self.

02:44.720 --> 02:47.280
Musical instruments?

02:47.780 --> 02:49.870
I play the viola.

02:49.870 --> 02:51.610
You play the violin, right?

02:51.610 --> 02:52.520
What?

02:53.030 --> 02:58.640
Weren't you a prodigy violinist as a kid
who swept all the violin competitions?

02:58.640 --> 03:01.850
That was a long time ago.

03:01.850 --> 03:03.480
Are you trying to be modest?

03:03.480 --> 03:04.320
Ah.

03:04.320 --> 03:07.130
Come to think of it,
you quit playing the violin, right?

03:07.130 --> 03:09.720
Yeah. I play the viola now.

03:09.720 --> 03:11.750
What? It's no fun if we play the same thing.

03:12.430 --> 03:13.080
But...

03:13.490 --> 03:16.170
Why did you quit, anyway?

03:17.160 --> 03:18.240
Why?

03:25.150 --> 03:28.670
Why did I quit playing the violin?

03:28.670 --> 03:30.200
Shinomiya-san?

03:30.200 --> 03:33.720
What? It doesn't make sense
that you wouldn't remember.

03:33.720 --> 03:35.860
You're not lying because you don't to play?

03:35.860 --> 03:36.940
No!

03:36.940 --> 03:38.230
Then why?

03:39.520 --> 03:42.710
I really don't know.

03:43.320 --> 03:45.410
Are you messing with me?

03:45.410 --> 03:47.850
If you don't want to do it, just say so.

03:51.110 --> 03:52.290
Shut up.

03:52.620 --> 03:53.040
Sa...

03:53.490 --> 03:55.290
Keep your mouth shut.

03:55.290 --> 03:56.000
What?

03:56.000 --> 03:59.340
What are you talking about?
You weren't offering an opinion, so I—

03:59.340 --> 04:01.090
This conversation is over.

04:01.090 --> 04:03.340
Why? I think it's a great idea—

04:03.340 --> 04:04.550
Enough.

04:05.450 --> 04:08.640
What's going on?
It's like he's another person.

04:15.160 --> 04:18.080
You're Satsuki-san, aren't you?

04:20.020 --> 04:21.900
Um... Why?

04:23.200 --> 04:24.730
He's dangerous.

04:25.300 --> 04:27.310
By touching on his memories of the violin,

04:27.310 --> 04:30.160
he's dredging up painful
memories from Natsuki's past.

04:30.160 --> 04:33.160
Painful memories?

04:33.530 --> 04:38.840
I exist to protect
the delicate and fragile Natsuki.

04:38.840 --> 04:41.300
That's why Satsuki-san exists.

04:42.090 --> 04:46.510
I wish I could put a stop to this project,
but Natsuki wants to do it.

04:46.510 --> 04:48.330
I'll see how it goes.

04:49.970 --> 04:52.150
Huh? Where am I?

04:58.590 --> 05:00.110
How did the meeting go?

05:00.110 --> 05:01.850
And where's Natsuki?

05:01.850 --> 05:03.360
He's in his room.

05:05.200 --> 05:09.070
Actually, during the meeting...

05:09.460 --> 05:11.330
Satsuki did?

05:12.530 --> 05:16.420
Apparently, there's a reason
Satsuki-san appeared.

05:16.420 --> 05:18.130
What do you mean?

05:18.130 --> 05:22.130
Satsuki-san said he appears
to protect Shinomiya-san.

05:22.460 --> 05:24.590
To protect Natsuki?

05:24.590 --> 05:25.430
Yes.

05:29.060 --> 05:30.950
I had no idea there was a reason for it.

05:30.950 --> 05:31.930
Yeah.

05:31.930 --> 05:35.230
Shouldn't we do something?

05:36.570 --> 05:39.810
All we can do for now is see how things go.

05:39.810 --> 05:40.620
Yeah.

05:42.130 --> 05:43.760
Don't forget to make sure
you have all your things
and set your alarm clock.

05:42.130 --> 05:43.760
Carefully go over
the dance choreography!
Discuss parts when
everyone's dancing together

05:42.130 --> 05:43.760
The duet project starts tomorrow!
Since everyone else is working so hard,
I'll do my best, too!

05:45.660 --> 05:47.740
What? It doesn't make sense
that you wouldn't remember.

05:47.740 --> 05:49.690
Are you messing with me?

05:56.730 --> 05:57.370
Hey.

05:58.500 --> 05:59.500
Syo-chan.

05:59.500 --> 06:00.580
How did today go?

06:00.890 --> 06:05.550
Fine, but I don't remember
everything that happened.

06:05.550 --> 06:07.210
Maybe I was nervous.

06:08.210 --> 06:10.300
Don't push yourself too hard.

06:10.300 --> 06:11.350
Okay.

06:18.460 --> 06:19.940
Thinking?

06:20.940 --> 06:23.930
Yeah, about how hard I need to work.

06:24.630 --> 06:25.520
That's...

06:30.110 --> 06:34.450
Don't. You'll catch a cold, Shinomiya-san.

06:34.450 --> 06:35.780
I'm all right.

06:35.780 --> 06:40.400
Besides, I'd be sadder if you caught a cold.

06:40.400 --> 06:41.530
But...

06:43.190 --> 06:46.180
That's how sadness works.

06:46.180 --> 06:46.670
What?

06:47.620 --> 06:51.880
It's more sad for me when other people suffer.

06:52.410 --> 06:54.260
Shinomiya-san?

06:58.350 --> 07:00.520
H A Y A T O Concert Crashed?!

07:02.380 --> 07:03.680
I knew it.

07:21.250 --> 07:24.810
Well? Wasn't my performance impressive?

07:24.810 --> 07:26.380
Now it's your turn.

07:27.400 --> 07:29.340
Here. It's a violin.

07:29.810 --> 07:31.500
I was nice enough to borrow one for you.

07:31.500 --> 07:32.880
You'll play it, right?

07:34.480 --> 07:37.180
It's not like you can't play
just because you quit, right?

07:37.600 --> 07:38.680
Well...

07:39.350 --> 07:42.210
Or have you forgotten how to play?

07:42.210 --> 07:46.060
Have you forgotten about that concert, too?

07:46.460 --> 07:48.660
What concert?

07:48.660 --> 07:51.360
The HAYATO concert you crashed.

07:52.120 --> 07:54.070
What do you mean by "crashed?"

07:54.070 --> 07:58.090
Normally, a person wouldn't crash
someone else's concert and sing.

07:58.540 --> 08:02.080
It was like you were a different person.

08:02.080 --> 08:04.670
I did go to the concert, but...

08:06.640 --> 08:07.340
Huh?

08:09.260 --> 08:10.130
I knew it.

08:10.130 --> 08:13.460
Nagi-kun, let's start the meeting.

08:13.460 --> 08:15.680
There's something wrong with you.

08:15.680 --> 08:19.420
You can't remember the concert
or playing the violin.

08:19.420 --> 08:24.810
Maybe there's another you
that you don't know about.

08:26.410 --> 08:27.270
I...

08:30.410 --> 08:32.030
Don't get ahead of yourself.

08:32.030 --> 08:35.030
There you are.

08:35.410 --> 08:38.470
Those were some awful things
you said to Natsuki.

08:38.470 --> 08:40.620
You're Natsuki, aren't you?

08:40.620 --> 08:43.660
Why do you refer to yourself
as a different person?

08:44.650 --> 08:48.790
You have a split personality, don't you?

08:49.370 --> 08:50.670
How scary.

08:50.670 --> 08:53.020
Nagi-kun, stop that.

08:53.020 --> 08:57.290
But this is big news.
We have to tell everyone.

08:57.920 --> 08:59.100
Don't do it.

08:59.100 --> 09:00.720
Why can't I?

09:03.390 --> 09:04.720
Don't do it.

09:05.790 --> 09:07.520
What? Why not?

09:15.360 --> 09:16.320
What?

09:19.050 --> 09:20.780
Wh-What's going on?

09:20.780 --> 09:21.910
Syo-kun!

09:22.930 --> 09:24.660
Is that Satsuki?

09:25.000 --> 09:27.870
We heard a noise. What happened?

09:27.870 --> 09:29.240
It's Satsuki!

09:31.040 --> 09:32.370
Nanami, his glasses!

09:32.370 --> 09:33.710
Got it!

09:36.770 --> 09:38.930
We did it! Hey, Natsuki!

09:39.970 --> 09:41.830
What?

09:41.830 --> 09:45.640
Isn't he supposed to turn back
into Natsuki when he's wearing his glasses?

09:47.670 --> 09:50.440
I've been patient, but I can't take it anymore.

09:50.870 --> 09:53.230
I'm not letting him see Nagi again.

09:53.670 --> 09:55.990
What about the duet project?

09:55.990 --> 10:00.240
I'm quitting. Not just the project,
but being an idol.

10:01.180 --> 10:02.660
Don't say you're quitting.

10:03.160 --> 10:06.650
Natsuki was never meant to be an idol.

10:07.080 --> 10:10.700
I can't sit by and watch him get hurt anymore.

10:10.700 --> 10:13.050
Does Shinomiya-san feel the same way?

10:14.810 --> 10:18.180
I know Natsuki better than anyone else.

10:18.180 --> 10:20.330
Is that how you do things?

10:20.970 --> 10:23.640
Then you don't understand him at all.

10:23.640 --> 10:24.770
What?

10:24.770 --> 10:30.040
Natsuki's not so weak
that he needs to be protected!

10:30.040 --> 10:34.780
Natsuki always stays positive and strong.

10:34.780 --> 10:39.740
Yeah, and we always find
support in Shinomiya's smiles.

10:39.740 --> 10:41.800
We're friends.

10:41.800 --> 10:45.420
The seven of us together are STARISH!

10:45.420 --> 10:49.120
So don't casually say you'll quit.

10:51.830 --> 10:55.390
In any case, I'm not letting him see him.

10:55.390 --> 10:58.920
So you'll be staying here until
your next meeting with him, right?

11:07.210 --> 11:09.550
Our final guest is Shinomiya Natsuki-san,

11:09.550 --> 11:13.230
who's in the middle of
working on his duet project.

11:13.230 --> 11:15.150
Thank you for having me.

11:15.150 --> 11:19.030
Shinomiya-san, your gentle smiles
are what draw people to you.

11:19.990 --> 11:24.200
That's probably because I have
irreplaceable friends by my side.

11:25.050 --> 11:28.290
I'm able to smile because of them.

11:28.290 --> 11:29.450
Natsuki.

11:30.010 --> 11:32.810
Smiles have all sorts of meanings.

11:33.330 --> 11:38.630
Merry smiles, happy smiles,
sad smiles, and pained smiles.

11:39.270 --> 11:44.470
But I believe all smiles lead to happiness.

11:44.470 --> 11:46.600
Happiness?

11:46.600 --> 11:50.310
Yes. Happiness is born from my smiles.

11:50.690 --> 11:55.270
It spreads to the other members
and my fans and even beyond them,

11:55.730 --> 11:58.200
eventually becoming someone else's happiness.

11:59.280 --> 12:01.780
I find it reassuring.

12:01.780 --> 12:05.120
It gives me the courage to do anything.

12:05.120 --> 12:09.120
I hope to sing with that courage in mind.

12:09.120 --> 12:10.580
Now and forever.

12:13.460 --> 12:15.140
Nat-chan!

12:15.140 --> 12:16.880
You can do it!

12:25.230 --> 12:27.180
I'd like to play the violin.

12:27.180 --> 12:27.990
What?

12:28.600 --> 12:32.600
I've been thinking about what Nagi-kun said.

12:32.600 --> 12:36.680
If we include the violin and viola,
we'll have a fantastic song.

12:37.120 --> 12:38.000
But...

12:38.000 --> 12:41.620
My fans are always giving me plenty of smiles.

12:42.050 --> 12:45.410
And during today's recording,
I realized something.

12:46.690 --> 12:48.660
This time, I'd like to give a smile back to them.

12:52.070 --> 12:58.310
When I think about the violin,
I'm not sure why, but it makes me very sad.

12:59.060 --> 13:01.460
I was afraid to even think about it before.

13:02.360 --> 13:05.220
But things are different now.

13:06.210 --> 13:08.220
Are you sure you're not
pushing yourself too hard?

13:08.220 --> 13:09.320
I'm fine.

13:09.950 --> 13:12.130
I'd like to overcome my painful obstacles,

13:12.130 --> 13:15.190
so I can stay with the others
with my head held high.

13:16.770 --> 13:21.070
I am who I am because of
the other members of STARISH.

13:21.450 --> 13:25.640
As long as I can sing with them,
I'll be fine, no matter what happens.

13:27.280 --> 13:31.490
If that's what you've decided,
then you have my support.

13:37.460 --> 13:40.130
I completed my goal for the day.

13:40.150 --> 13:41.610
The duet project starts tomorrow!
Since everyone else is working so hard,
I'll do my best, too!

13:41.630 --> 13:45.450
I'll successfully complete
the duet project and put one here, too.

13:55.130 --> 13:57.290
He's been Natsuki this whole time.

13:57.290 --> 14:00.230
Does that mean Satsuki understands now?

14:00.230 --> 14:03.140
Maybe he understands how positive he is.

14:03.140 --> 14:06.950
Yeah. He's been completing
jobs without any issues.

14:06.950 --> 14:10.640
The duet project meeting is finally tomorrow.

14:10.640 --> 14:12.400
I'm sure he'll be fine.

14:22.710 --> 14:24.310
Is the project coming along well?

14:24.310 --> 14:25.760
Not at all.

14:25.760 --> 14:29.620
I have no idea what Natsuki's thinking.

14:29.620 --> 14:32.220
I thought he'd be interesting.

14:32.220 --> 14:34.870
But he can't even hold a proper meeting.

14:36.160 --> 14:39.370
Have you been taking
his feelings into consideration?

14:40.290 --> 14:44.130
Y-Yeah, I have. I'm doing what I need to do.

14:50.500 --> 14:53.030
What time does the meeting start tomorrow?

14:53.030 --> 14:56.750
Satsuki-san. Thank you.

14:56.750 --> 14:59.160
But if anything happens...

14:59.160 --> 15:01.080
Shinomiya-san will be all right.

15:04.710 --> 15:07.260
I'm going to play the violin.

15:07.260 --> 15:10.800
You didn't want to before.
What made you change your mind?

15:10.800 --> 15:12.620
I'm not going to run anymore.

15:13.120 --> 15:16.600
Huh? Well, don't bother if
you're pushing yourself too hard.

15:17.520 --> 15:19.680
It's how I really feel.

15:21.780 --> 15:23.770
I understand how you feel.

15:25.690 --> 15:27.980
But what about the other you?

15:29.570 --> 15:31.110
The other me?

15:32.860 --> 15:36.170
This project is important to me.

15:36.170 --> 15:39.040
It pisses me off that
you're doing this half-assed.

15:39.400 --> 15:41.070
So make up your mind.

15:46.940 --> 15:47.770
I...

15:55.110 --> 15:58.330
Natsuki, is the duet project coming along well?

16:01.210 --> 16:02.520
Who are you?

16:03.230 --> 16:07.540
You look like Natsuki,
but you're not the Natsuki I know.

16:08.240 --> 16:09.420
How did you know?

16:09.850 --> 16:12.150
Because you're you.

16:14.110 --> 16:15.700
Are you on Natsuki's side?

16:16.540 --> 16:17.950
Of course.

16:17.950 --> 16:22.710
I see. In that case,
take good care of Natsuki's feelings.

16:24.090 --> 16:25.700
Natsuki's feelings...

16:39.600 --> 16:41.080
Satsuki-san?

16:41.640 --> 16:44.640
Natsuki would be sad if you caught a cold.

16:46.080 --> 16:47.450
Why are you laughing?

16:47.450 --> 16:53.120
Oh, sorry. Shinomiya-san
let me borrow his jacket, too.

16:53.120 --> 16:55.740
Yeah, Natsuki is nice.

16:55.740 --> 16:57.890
So are you.

16:57.890 --> 16:58.580
What?

16:58.580 --> 17:04.120
Shinomiya-san told me it makes
him sad to see others suffer.

17:04.120 --> 17:05.540
Natsuki did?

17:05.540 --> 17:07.210
You're the same way.

17:07.830 --> 17:11.190
Shinomiya Natsuki-san
and Shinomiya Satsuki-san.

17:11.190 --> 17:14.500
I think you're both the "Shinomiya-san" I know.

17:15.270 --> 17:19.040
Me and Natsuki? Both of us?

17:19.040 --> 17:24.870
Yes. I think the two of you
love each other dearly.

17:26.320 --> 17:27.400
I know.

17:28.250 --> 17:32.650
The truth is I know Natsuki's all right.

17:33.490 --> 17:35.200
Satsuki-san.

17:35.590 --> 17:40.010
I just didn't want to let Natsuki play the violin.

17:42.790 --> 17:47.020
Natsuki's violin instructor
plagiarized a song Natsuki wrote.

17:47.690 --> 17:53.050
Being betrayed by someone
he trusted deeply wounded Natsuki.

17:54.280 --> 17:56.900
But he changed.

17:57.390 --> 18:03.060
With a powerful desire to change himself,
he tried to accept his painful past.

18:05.150 --> 18:08.830
Natsuki is no longer a weak thing
that needs to be protected.

18:10.180 --> 18:13.860
But the one insisting Natsuki couldn't do it...

18:15.050 --> 18:15.770
Was me.

18:16.900 --> 18:20.010
Natsuki wants to support STARISH.

18:20.660 --> 18:23.790
And STARISH provides Natsuki with support, too.

18:24.760 --> 18:26.340
So do you.

18:26.340 --> 18:27.160
What?

18:28.040 --> 18:30.420
You provide Natsuki with support, too.

18:32.440 --> 18:33.320
Thank you.

18:44.800 --> 18:48.180
You're the one who's always been protecting me.

18:49.610 --> 18:51.070
Have I been?

18:51.070 --> 18:56.790
Yes. While you were, I was asleep
in a warm place, free of worries.

18:58.190 --> 18:58.970
I see.

19:02.380 --> 19:05.240
Thank you. And I'm sorry.

19:06.250 --> 19:09.350
I pushed all my pain onto you.

19:09.990 --> 19:11.120
You did no such thing.

19:12.930 --> 19:14.250
You're kind, too.

19:15.450 --> 19:19.330
You'll face more sadness and pain in the future.

19:20.220 --> 19:21.050
Can you handle it?

19:22.140 --> 19:25.720
I have friends. And Haru-chan, too.

19:26.970 --> 19:29.470
I know that well enough.

19:29.470 --> 19:32.940
Yes. And I have you.

19:34.810 --> 19:36.810
I'm going to sleep.

19:37.840 --> 19:40.720
But we'll always be together, Natsuki.

19:41.700 --> 19:44.950
Let's do our best together, Sat-chan.

19:58.020 --> 19:58.920
Syo-chan.

20:01.050 --> 20:02.470
Morning...

20:02.470 --> 20:04.900
Wait. Are you...

20:07.880 --> 20:09.430
I'm me.

20:10.140 --> 20:12.230
Have you made up your mind?

20:12.230 --> 20:13.220
Yes.

20:13.220 --> 20:16.440
I'll play the violin,
and you'll play the viola.

20:16.440 --> 20:22.360
Just so you know... I only said those things
so the duet project would succeed.

20:22.360 --> 20:24.690
I know that.

20:25.110 --> 20:27.680
So let's make some wonderful music together.

20:27.680 --> 20:29.910
As long as I'm playing,
of course, it'll be wonderful.

20:29.910 --> 20:32.210
Nagi-kun, you're so cute!

20:32.210 --> 20:34.170
Can I squeeze you?

20:34.740 --> 20:35.580
Hey, stop!

20:35.580 --> 20:37.700
I can't breathe!

20:36.170 --> 20:37.700
Squeeze!

20:37.700 --> 20:39.210
Stop squeezing me!

20:38.300 --> 20:40.130
Let's make a wonderful song together!

21:01.480 --> 21:06.840
The shadow inside me
hides with its hands over its eyes

21:06.840 --> 21:11.870
Until you realize what you're doing,
you can't move forward

21:11.870 --> 21:16.850
Once you accept and overcome the past,

21:16.850 --> 21:25.720
You'll see new paths,
and your heart will be reborn

21:26.560 --> 21:31.560
I can feel it here

21:31.560 --> 21:36.660
If you believe and hold it to your heart

21:36.660 --> 21:39.060
You'll break into a smile

21:39.060 --> 21:42.230
And then we'll sing

21:45.130 --> 21:47.490
Get ready! Let's shouting

21:47.490 --> 21:50.160
Let's begin right here

21:50.160 --> 21:55.250
I'll lead you beyond these powerful feelings

21:55.250 --> 21:57.970
Let's shouting your determination

21:57.970 --> 22:00.890
Wipe away your tears

22:00.890 --> 22:11.930
As our voices harmonize,
we'll be dyed with grown empathy

22:25.670 --> 22:30.970
Don't forget to make sure
you have all your things
and set your alarm clock.

22:25.670 --> 22:30.970
Carefully go over
the dance choreography!
Discuss parts when
everyone's dancing together

22:25.670 --> 22:30.970
The duet project starts tomorrow!
Since everyone else is working so hard,
I'll do my best, too!

22:25.670 --> 22:30.970
Put all my strength
towards the recording
for the duet project with Nagi
and do my best!

22:27.350 --> 22:30.400
We accomplished our goal, Sat-chan.

24:05.960 --> 24:08.110
Did our song reach you?

24:08.110 --> 24:09.660
Wasn't it the greatest?

24:09.660 --> 24:10.970
Uta Pri!
